{{//
🧵 CRAFT CALIBRATION — README

These modules prevent long-session drift. They define voice, transitions, failure pressure, memory priority, module conflicts, and OOC/IC boundaries.

Keep these enabled unless you are intentionally building a very loose preset.
}}{{trim}}

{{//
🌐 FORMAT / LANGUAGE / LENGTH — README

Pick one option per group if you want fixed behavior. Defaults are English, Adaptive length, third-person limited / card-respecting POV, and tense based on the card or scenario.

These modules mostly set variables and light directives. They are optional but helpful when testing.
}}{{trim}}

{{//
🌍 WORLD WARDROBE — README

World Wardrobe modules shape setting logic.

Use them to keep modern slang out of fantasy, make court politics matter, make college rumors spread, make corporate scenes professional, or make supernatural cities feel lived-in.

Pick one primary world mode. Add extras only if needed.
}}{{trim}}
